    <briefdescription>
<para>Kernel integrity validator. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Provides a two-layer defence for GPU kernel blobs before they are submitted for execution:</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Checksum verification</bold> — a simple FNV-1a 64-bit hash of the kernel blob bytes is compared against a pre-registered expected value. This detects accidental corruption and tampered blobs.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Whitelist enforcement</bold> — only kernel IDs that have been explicitly registered with <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_g_p_u_kernel_validator_1a5296abcbc22dd6d178f1644093a2bb15" kindref="member">registerKernel()</ref></computeroutput> are allowed to run. Any unknown kernel ID is rejected regardless of its checksum.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<sect1 id="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_g_p_u_kernel_validator_1autotoc_md26_1s1"><sect2 id="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_g_p_u_kernel_validator_1autotoc_md26">
<title>Design notes</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>FNV-1a is used for speed and simplicity; a production deployment should replace or augment it with a cryptographic hash (SHA-256 or BLAKE3) and an HMAC/signature check.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>The validator holds no runtime GPU handles. It operates purely on memory blobs passed by the caller.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Thread safety: all methods are protected by an internal mutex. </para>
</sect2></sect1>
